Prossh makes a 0/1 Kobold for every mana you spend casting it, so a six-mana Prossh is a dragon plus six sacrifice fodder. Every Kobold dying is damage, cards or mana in this deck. Food Chain turns that into an infinite loop: exile Prossh and the Kobolds for mana, recast Prossh for more Kobolds, and make more mana each time. With a damage payoff out, the table dies to Kobolds entering.

# The commander
Prossh, Skyraider of Kher :: six mana, flying. When you CAST him, create X 0/1 Kobolds named Kobolds of Kher Keep, where X is the mana spent. Sacrifice another creature: Prossh gets +1/+0.
The Kobolds come from casting, not from entering, so a countered Prossh still leaves you the Kobolds. Commander tax raises X: the second cast makes eight, the third ten.
Prossh is his own sacrifice outlet. Sacrificing Kobolds to pump him also triggers every death payoff below.

# Infinite combos — why this is Bracket 3.5
Prossh, Skyraider of Kher + Food Chain :: exile Prossh to Food Chain for 7 mana (his mana value 6, plus 1) and send him to the command zone. Recast him; the Kobolds equal everything you spent, tax included. Exile each Kobold for 1 mana. Each loop makes 5 more mana than it costs, so unlimited Kobolds and unlimited mana for creature spells. With Impact Tremors, Purphoros or Agate Instigator out, every Kobold entering damages each opponent; with Beast Whisperer, every Prossh cast draws.
Squee, the Immortal + Food Chain :: exile Squee for 4 mana, recast him from exile for 3. One mana of profit per loop: unlimited creature mana and unlimited Squee entering.
Chatterfang, Squirrel General + Pitiless Plunderer :: each death makes a Treasure, Chatterfang adds a Squirrel, and Chatterfang's own ability sacrifices the Squirrel for {B}. Unlimited deaths.
Prossh, Skyraider of Kher + Phyrexian Altar + Purphoros, God of the Forge :: sacrifice Kobolds to the Altar to recast Prossh from the command zone; Purphoros deals 2 to each opponent for every Kobold that enters.
Warren Soultrader + Chatterfang, Squirrel General + Zulaport Cutthroat :: Soultrader turns a Squirrel into a Treasure plus a Squirrel; every loop drains the table. Blood Artist works in place of the Cutthroat.
Food Chain mana only casts creatures. That is all the loop needs (Prossh and Squee are creatures), but the damage has to come from triggers, not from spells.

# Payoffs — what makes the Kobolds lethal
Impact Tremors :: each creature entering deals 1 to each opponent.
Purphoros, God of the Forge :: each other creature entering deals 2 to each opponent.
Agate Instigator :: each other creature entering deals 1 to each opponent.
Mirkwood Bats :: each token created or sacrificed drains each opponent 1.
Goblin Bombardment :: sacrifice a creature: 1 damage to any target.
Mayhem Devil :: every permanent ANY player sacrifices deals 1 damage. Treasures and Food count.
Zulaport Cutthroat :: each creature of yours that dies drains each opponent 1.
Blood Artist :: any creature dying drains a player 1.
Grave Pact :: every creature you sacrifice costs each opponent a creature.
Korvold, Fae-Cursed King :: every permanent you sacrifice is a card and a +1/+1 counter.
Sephiroth, Fabled SOLDIER :: drains on every other creature's death, and draws on sacrifice.

# Sacrifice outlets and mana
Phyrexian Altar :: a creature for one mana of any colour.
Ashnod's Altar :: a creature for {C}{C}.
Viscera Seer :: free, scry 1.
Warren Soultrader :: pay 1 life and sacrifice for a Treasure.
Pitiless Plunderer :: a Treasure whenever another creature of yours dies.
Phyrexian Tower :: a land that sacrifices for {B}{B}.
Gaea's Cradle :: {G} per creature. After one Prossh, that is seven or more.
Culling the Weak :: sacrifice for {B}{B}{B}{B}.
Skullclamp :: a Kobold becomes two cards.
Village Rites :: sacrifice for two cards.
Fecundity :: every creature that dies draws its controller a card. It's symmetric, so your Kobolds draw you far more.
Beast Whisperer :: a card for every creature spell you cast.

# Tutor lines — what to fetch, and when
Demonic Tutor -> Food Chain :: the missing half when Prossh is already castable.
Vampiric Tutor -> Food Chain :: instant, on top: cast it at an opponent's end step and draw it.
Beseech the Mirror -> Food Chain :: bargain a Kobold or Treasure to cast Food Chain free.
Diabolic Intent -> Impact Tremors :: sacrifice a Kobold for any card; take a payoff if Food Chain is out.
Chord of Calling -> Squee, the Immortal :: instant speed, convoked by Kobolds.
Finale of Devastation -> Purphoros, God of the Forge :: Purphoros is an enchantment creature card, so Finale finds it: X = 4 puts it onto the battlefield (as an enchantment until you have five red devotion). X = 3 finds Squee instead.
Eldritch Evolution -> Pitiless Plunderer :: sacrifice a two-drop for a four-drop.
Noxious Revival -> Food Chain :: puts a destroyed Food Chain back on top of your library.
Eternal Witness -> Food Chain :: returns it to hand.

# Mana
Llanowar Elves :: the usual.
Elvish Mystic :: the second copy.
Fyndhorn Elves :: the third.
Elves of Deep Shadow :: black mana.
Birds of Paradise :: any colour.
Ignoble Hierarch :: black, red or green.
Delighted Halfling :: mana that makes Prossh uncounterable.
Deathrite Shaman :: mana from lands in graveyards.
Elvish Spirit Guide :: a free {G}.
Simian Spirit Guide :: a free {R}.
Sakura-Tribe Elder :: a basic land, and fodder.
Sol Ring :: the usual.
Arcane Signet :: the usual.
Talisman of Impulse :: red or green.
Lotus Petal :: free.
Dark Ritual :: {B}{B}{B}.
Farseek :: a dual, tapped.
Nature's Lore :: a Forest-type dual, untapped.
Three Visits :: the same.
Wheel of Fortune :: refill.
Sylvan Library :: pick the best of three every turn.
Phyrexian Arena :: a card every upkeep.

# Protection and answers
Lightning Greaves :: haste for Prossh to swing with a pumped flier.
Hexing Squelcher :: your spells can't be countered; your creatures have ward (pay 2 life).
Veil of Summer :: protection from blue and black for a turn.
Deflecting Swat :: free while Prossh is out: redirect removal.
Deadly Rollick :: free while Prossh is out: exile a creature.
Pyroblast :: counter a blue spell or destroy a blue permanent.
Red Elemental Blast :: the same.
Abrupt Decay :: uncounterable removal for anything with mana value 3 or less.
Assassin's Trophy :: destroy any permanent.
Culling Ritual :: destroys every nonland permanent with mana value 2 or less, your Kobolds included, and adds a mana for each.
Boseiju, Who Endures :: a land that destroys an artifact, enchantment or nonbasic land.
Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer :: Treasure and a stolen card on every hit.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep mana dorks or rituals that cast Prossh by turn four, and one of Food Chain, a tutor, or a payoff. A turn-four Prossh is six Kobolds and a Gaea's Cradle that taps for seven.
Without Food Chain, Prossh plus Impact Tremors and an Altar still deals a lot: every cast is a wave of damage, and every recast after removal makes more Kobolds.
With Food Chain out, put a payoff down first, then go: the loop doesn't stop until the table is dead.
